<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Salvador</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Salvador is a city on the north-eastern coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brazil">Brazil</a>, founded in 1549 by the first Governor-General, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tome-de-sousa">Tomé de Sousa</a>. It served as the capital of Portuguese colonial Brazil until 1763 and was a major centre of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sugar-plantation">sugar</a> economy and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/atlantic-slave-trade">Atlantic slave trade</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/portuguese-empire">Portuguese Empire</a> profile treats its foundation as the start of a more systematic colonial administration in Brazil.</p></div>
